        "Alumina or platinum crucibles"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "not_available": [
    {
      "technique": "X-ray Diffraction (XRD)",
      "why_useful": "XRD is the gold standard for directly measuring the crystalline structure and amorphous content of polymers, which would complement the thermal data from DSC."
    }
  ],
  "clarifying_question": null,
  "summary": "To determine the crystallinity of your PEEK material, Differential Scanning Calorimetry (DSC) is the most appropriate technique available. By measuring the melting enthalpy, you can calculate the crystalline fraction. Please note that DSC is a destructive thermal analysis method, and you should confirm that the DSC pans available are rated for the high melting temperature of PEEK."
}

